WEBVTT

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.400
There! I win!

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.370
Wow, you got me, Emilia.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.410
Since when did you get so good at games?

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.000
I don't know, Dad, maybe you got worse.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.500
What can I say?

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.540
I didn't think there were
game cafés like this in Japan.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.450
Yes, it's a wonderful place.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.200
But you know what else, Dad?

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.870
Something nicer happened.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.620
Oh, what is that?

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.120
I think there are other high school girls
who love board games here in Japan!

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.160
That's when I decided...

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.120
...to become a game author myself!

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.830
That's my dream!

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.700
Really? That's interesting.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.620
I know, right?

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.870
It's quite rare for you to bring a companion.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.410
A friend, perhaps?

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.750
I wouldn't use such a strong word with him.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:14.080
More like "someone I'm stuck with."

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.450
You must have known
each other for a long time.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.410
I guess so. Since the Okinawa days...

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:22.200
How long ago was that?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.540
We were in the camp 15 years ago.
Getting senile already?

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:30.290
Huh? Did you say something,
annoying four-eyes?

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.870
I see that you're politeness is still intact.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.290
What?

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:38.540
Who do you have to thank for
introducing you to board games?

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.000
Did you forget that, too?

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.870
A game buddy, as I thought.
So has he been to Saikoro Club, too?

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.700
Saikoro...? What about dice?

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.040
It's the name of my store.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.120
Store...?

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.290
I run a board game shop now.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.750
That's the first time I've heard that.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.910
It's the first time I've told you.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:01.160
Well, there's nothing
there you'd find interesting.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.500
Don't worry, I wasn't
interested in the first place.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.660
It's fruitless as a business
opportunity anyway.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.120
What...?

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.700
Board games don't make any money in Japan.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.910
Titles that become bestsellers in
Germany make very little money here.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:21.160
Japan is still very far
behind in board game culture.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.370
You should know that very well.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.580
That's...!

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:28.250
In fact, I don't count on
the Japanese market at all.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.830
Market...?

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:33.040
Of course, I do some business in Japan.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.540
But there's nothing here
worth me visiting in person.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.540
Over ten years have passed
and you're still as annoying as ever.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.910
What you said is true.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.040
Digital games were too bright a light in Japan,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.160
and board games were hidden
in the shadows for too long.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:03:00.080
But the Japanese are catching onto
the fact that this incredible thing exists...

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.620
Listen to me.
Japanese board games have a future.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.410
My shop, the market, and our designers!

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.660
I see, the market and designers...

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.450
Yeah, remember that, George!

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.200
Huh? George?

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.080
Wait... could you possibly be...?

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.200
Even after the trip to Kanazawa
with Aya-chan and Midori-chan,

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.690
there's still plenty of
summer vacation left for us.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:06.770
Today, the three of us are...

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.440
Playtesting?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.790
Wait, your original game is finished?!

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.290
No, it's still just a prototype.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:20.700
I'm going to show the manager and
get his feedback, then do some brushing up.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:24.080
That said, I guess it's already
taking shape, somewhat.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.620
Wow, really?!

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:27.540
Yes...

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:29.450
Awesome! I wanna play!

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.080
Let me try! Let me try your game!

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.580
N-No! It's incomplete...

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.540
Huh? Why not? You want to
play too, right, Miki-chan?

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.370
Um, yeah...

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:43.790
See? Come on, please? Hey, Midori-chan!

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.870
I said no!

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.200
Oh... Sorry...

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:55.250
But I don't want to show
people anything incomplete.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.160
What do you think, Manager?

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.620
Hmm...

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:11.630
Midori-chan, have you let
anyone else play this game yet?

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:18.750
No, of course not. It's not even finished yet.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.950
I see, just as I thought...

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.290
As you thought?

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.200
What do you mean, Manager?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.450
Manager!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.000
Well, this is...

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.290
Sorry, we're closed for the day...

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.750
Did I interrupt you?

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.080
You...! What are you doing here?!

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.830
Oh, is this someone you know?

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:47.790
So this is your place.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:50.910
You said you had no interest.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:55.660
I changed my mind.
I thought I should take a look.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.700
Hmm?

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:00.790
Is that a new game? Let me play.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.870
It's still just a prototype...

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:06.160
Oh, are you the designer of this game?

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.330
Yes... I am.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.370
What's your name?

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.750
Um, Manager? Who is this gentleman...?

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.250
Oh, yeah, he's--

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:17.410
My apologies, it was rude of me
not to introduce myself first.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:24.000
I am George Beresford. I am the
representative and designer for Bad Dwarf.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.410
Bad Dwarf?! You're...?!

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:32.120
I see you did your research, as always.
I'm impressed that you know this idiot.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.870
W-What?! Come on, Manager!

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:39.450
It's Bad Dwarf! They're the famous
new game brand from the US!

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:44.250
They're famous for high-quality
games rated highly by critics!

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.620
And you are?

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.330
Um, yes, I'm Ono Midori.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:53.540
Midori, don't you want
people to play your game?

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.410
It's not like that...

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.790
It's just that this one isn't complete yet...

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:01.950
It's not ready to be played by people...

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:06.120
But you were playing it with
Takeru just now. It must be ready.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.620
Well... that's...

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:12.830
This is an opportunity, sure... but...

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:18.370
You can say no. You don't owe him anything.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:21.830
Midori, why hesitate? Are you afraid?

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:22.870
Huh...?

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:28.200
You're scared that someone will
tell you your game is boring. Correct?

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.810
N-No, that's...

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.400
Hey, George!

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.450
I understand. I've had enough.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:35.120
Huh?

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.120
To be honest,

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.820
I didn't expect there to be a young
designer like you here in Japan.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:45.250
That's why I was interested in what
kind of game you'd design, but...

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.200
...I'm sorry.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:49.250
Sorry? What do you mean...

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.540
You're not a designer.

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:58.000
A designer should want to have
their game played more than anything.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.700
Hey, George!

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.290
Why...

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:05.540
Why would someone I just
met talk to me like that?!

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:11.200
If you can't let other people
play it, it's not a game.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.790
I said it's not finished yet!

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:16.500
Once it's done, of course
I'll have people play it...

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.660
Then when will it be finished?

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:22.700
When...? That's... I mean, soon...

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.370
I'm sorry to break it to you,
but that game will never be complete.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.660
You'll never get anywhere if you're
just stuck inside your own head.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:34.540
You will be an old lady and
it will still be incomplete.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:38.700
Remember this: A game cannot be built alone.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:44.330
Can't be built alone...?

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:49.370
No... a game is a work of art by an author!

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:52.910
Games are created by an author's talent!

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:04.790
That guy will eat his words...

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:08.160
Not even when I'm an old lady, did he say?

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:10.330
I'll show him!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:17.960
{Between}

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:27.430
Midori-chan?

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:39.160
Coming!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:40.020
Welcome--

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:46.110
What's wrong with your face, Midori-chan?!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.950
Huge bags under your eyes...!

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:52.660
I, uh, want you to try something...

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:53.750
Huh?

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.040
Try? Try what?

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.410
My, ah...

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.370
Ah?

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:01.290
Ah...

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:01.830
Alligator?

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:02.800
No!

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:04.700
So then, what?

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.500
Well, the, uh...

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.330
Come on, what is it?!

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.750
I want you to try my game!

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.250
What?!

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:16.370
But you said it's still a prototype.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:21.540
Yeah! You got all mad, like, "I said no!"

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.200
I, um...

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.000
Is there a reason why you're in a hurry?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:33.120
Well, last night, at Saikoro Club...

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:39.250
Wow, that really happened?!

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.580
So then what, Midori-chan?

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:45.700
So I pulled an all-nighter.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:51.080
I wanted you two to playtest
this as soon as humanly possible.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:54.200
The game is called <i>One Room</i>.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:59.950
You work to make money, buy furniture
and trinkets, and design a room that you like.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:02.580
Wow! It really is a game!

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:03.020
Huh...?

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:04.650
So many pieces of furniture!

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:08.330
Did you draw all of these?
You're a great artist!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.290
Really? Thanks...

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:15.330
An interior design game, huh?
That sounds super fun.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:19.040
Yeah, this type of thing is a girl's dream.

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:23.080
Okay, here are the rules.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:27.620
You start with your room board and five gold.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:28.660
Five gold?

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:32.750
Oh, gold is the unit of currency,
like yen or dollars.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.250
Gotcha.

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.950
The game is composed of two phases.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.950
The first phase is the work phase.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:43.410
You choose how many hours of work you
want to do from the cards available.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:44.750
A poker deck...?

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:49.950
I didn't have time to make the
number cards, so this is a substitute.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:53.160
The numbers on these
cards represent labor hours.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.290
Three for three hours?

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.120
Yes.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:57.700
I see!

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:04.410
The starting player picks first and
gets money equal to the number of hours.

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:07.410
So if I pick an eight, I get eight gold?

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:08.660
That's right.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:12.870
Okay, so it's best to pick the biggest number!

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:16.700
Yes, you get the most money that way.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:17.750
But...

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:18.830
Huh?

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:24.540
...the player that picks the biggest number
can't go shopping in the next phase.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:25.950
Shopping?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.580
After the work phase
is the shopping phase.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:32.660
You can purchase any of the four pieces
of furniture available to put in your room.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:37.950
Like I said, the person who worked
the longest can't buy anything.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:40.750
On the other hand,
the person who worked the least

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.040
can start buying first
and can buy as much as they want.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.370
Oh, I get it!

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:48.120
You get out of work early
so you can go shopping sooner!

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:53.870
Yeah, that's the idea. So when you
buy furniture, you put it in your room.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:56.410
You can buy a maximum of 12 things.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:59.580
When any one player places 12 things
in their room, the game is over.

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:01.790
The person who scores the most points wins.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:04.330
How do you determine score?

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:07.950
Do you see the colored triangle on
the top right of each furniture tile?

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.370
Oh, yeah.

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:14.080
There are four different colors of furniture,
and each color represents a style.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:19.450
Pink is Asian, blue is Nordic, and so on.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:24.700
You get more points for having
more furniture in the same style.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.540
You see the numbers on
the right of the room board?

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:30.160
Those are the bonus points you get for having
multiple pieces of furniture in the same style.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:33.700
I see, so if you have seven, you get 28 points.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:38.500
Yes, but getting more than that won't
get you any additional points.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.700
That's the basic "furniture point" score.

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:44.750
In addition, you get a bonus
for buying trinkets.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:45.660
Trinkets...?

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:46.650
Bonus?

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:50.230
Trinkets have a grey triangle
on the bottom right corner.

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:54.290
These only give you one point
if you buy them individually,

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:58.040
but they give you three points if you put
them together with a certain other thing.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:02.500
For example, this cushion is worth
three points if you own a sofa.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.370
I see! What else is there?

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:08.620
The laptop goes with the desk,
and the books go with the bookshelf.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:12.760
Ooh, a board game! This goes with a table!

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:18.090
Furniture that costs more has
more trinkets that pair with it.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.540
Wow!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.700
You've thought this through.

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:26.410
So that's the overview. What do you think?

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.870
This is great! It seems like
a lot of fun, Midori-chan!

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:34.120
Yes! I can't wait to try it!

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.870
R-Really?

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:42.500
Yes! The game belongs to the author!
It's created by the author's talent!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.660
I'll prove that!

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.700
Come on, let's try!

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:47.540
Yeah!

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:50.540
Y-Yes! Well, for starters...

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:53.500
...Aya, pick a card and decide
how long you want to work!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.160
Yes!

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.700
Hmm... What to do...

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:15.790
I do want the board game, but
then I'd have to get the table, too...

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:18.990
Wait, the table costs how much?! Eleven gold!

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:21.750
Midori-chan, isn't this too expensive?!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:26.330
I had to set it high.
Tables support so many different trinkets.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.750
Grr...

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:31.410
I want to get a sofa, but
I can't find the right color...

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.830
Yeah, you don't want to miss
that sweet bonus score!

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:37.330
That would be important.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.790
Aya, it seems like you're
combining things well.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:42.500
Yep, I got the rules down perfectly!

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:45.790
Okay, your turn to pick work hours again.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:48.540
Hmm, I might have overspent...

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:50.580
In that case...

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:51.870
...this one!

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:54.700
Okay, I'll go with a nine.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.120
I'll take the four.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.410
Next is the shopping phase,
and Aya skips her shopping turn.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.370
Why?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.200
You worked the longest, remember?

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.330
Oh, right! I forgot...

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.540
Are you okay? I thought
you knew the rules perfectly.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.540
Um, yeah...

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:18.290
Okay, that's the end of the game.

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:25.000
Aya got 30 points, Miki 26, and I got 39 points.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:37.410
So, um... what did you think? Not very good?

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:41.160
Oh, uh... It was fun! Right, Miki-chan?!

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.500
Y-Yes!

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:47.410
Oh, no... They're obviously
trying to be nice to me...!

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:52.160
Please! I need you to be
brutally honest! I won't get mad!

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.160
Miki! Aya!

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:57.830
Okay...

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:59.330
In that case...

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:03.080
Um... It's not entirely
boring or anything, but...

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:05.790
...compared to the games
we've played up until now,

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:08.160
it feels like it's missing something...

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:12.160
It feels kind of monotonous
when you actually play it...

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:14.200
Monotonous...!

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:18.660
All the trinkets are the same points,
but maybe they should be different.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.000
Oh, I thought so, too!

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.540
Also, I'm always worried about the points,

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:26.450
so it didn't feel like I was
designing my dream home.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:30.910
Yeah! I had to give up on a thing I felt
was cute because it had the wrong color.

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:31.870
Also...

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:33.540
I know! Pets!

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:34.420
Pets?!

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:37.000
If this were my room, I'd love to have a pet!

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:42.970
Cat

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:39.540
Like seven points for a cat!

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:42.950
Oh, but maybe it would claw up the
Asian furniture, so negative seven for that!

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.510
Oh, but maybe it would claw up the
Asian furniture, so negative seven for that!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.510
Asian

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:46.370
That could be fun!

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:50.950
How about, like, a "chance card"
that would change up the flow a little?

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:53.410
Yeah, like trading furniture with someone!

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:54.910
That sounds fun!

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:58.080
Just putting the furniture on
the board is a bit boring, too.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:01.160
Yeah, I wonder if we can get creative and...

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:08.250
Oh, sorry, we're just amateurs, so...

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:13.330
Yeah, we must be saying something
completely off the mark, so don't worry...

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:18.870
What are you talking about?
Off the mark? You're spot on!

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:25.370
How can they find so many improvements
in just one playthrough...?

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:28.790
A game cannot be built alone.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.950
Midori-chan...?

00:19:30.950 --> 00:19:31.910
What else?

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.000
Huh?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:34.830
What else? Give me more!

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:36.830
Oh! We're sorry!

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:38.700
We went too far!

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:41.370
Anything! Tell me everything!

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:44.700
I put in so much thought, too...

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:49.540
I put in so much effort
to finish this all by myself.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:53.450
I was certain there was nothing
more I could do to improve this,

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:58.870
but... the result is...
I hate to admit it, but he's right.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:04.620
This game is far from complete, but...

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:08.370
We broke Midori-chan?!

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:12.410
My game can be so much more interesting!

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:17.290
I have to admit, I owe you one for this, George.

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:18.160
Hmm?

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.330
About Midori-chan.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:21.700
Oh, yeah...

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:24.540
I was supposed to be the one
to tell her what you told her.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:28.870
I made you become the bad guy. I'm sorry.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.250
You've always been soft on women.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.540
That said, I just did what I wanted to do.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:40.790
The designer's talents
create the game. That's true.

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:43.700
But it takes a village.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:44.750
Yeah...

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:46.910
Even the most talented genius designer

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:51.290
goes through countless testing sessions
before a game is complete.

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:57.000
All designers know how important it is
to have someone else play your game.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.660
You can't become a designer
while being afraid of criticism.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.160
Yeah...

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:06.910
What's important is whether or not
that girl can take the first step.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:11.830
If there is too much pride,
it can be an inhibitor to growth.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.200
Welcome--

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:18.120
Hey, Midori-chan?!

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.830
Mr. Beresford...

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.540
...you really are a professional.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:26.080
Everything you said was correct.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:30.080
I can't complete this game alone...

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.380
Midori-chan...

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:36.950
But... I won't give up! I'm not alone!

00:21:36.950 --> 00:21:41.830
I will definitely make a game!
Something that can make everyone smile!

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:52.790
She's so full of surprises.
I guess you really hit a nerve there.

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:56.910
Now it's getting interesting.

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:00.500
Cheers!

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.050
To a newborn...

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.620
...fledgling designer!

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:39.590
Playing a game alone with Maki-chan.

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:42.390
Before I knew it,
we were deep in conversation.

00:23:43.220 --> 00:23:46.230
I know that I'm a weakling...
